# Allowlist for the tracked-tree secret scan (PRODUCT-AUDIT P-30).
#
# `hachi security-audit --scan-tree` scans every git-tracked file with the
# credential patterns from `hachi/core/secret_scanner.py`. The entries below
# are the deliberate, obviously-fake fixtures the test suite plants so the
# redaction and credential-handling code has something to catch. They are
# not credentials and must never become credentials.
#
# Format — one entry per line, and this is the ONLY accepted form:
#   path:kind:fingerprint
# The fingerprint is the first 12 hex chars of the SHA-256 of the exact
# fixture value (see `hachi.core.secret_scanner.secret_fingerprint`). An
# entry suppresses that one occurrence only: a different credential of the
# same kind in the same file still trips the gate. Bare paths, directory
# prefixes, and path:kind entries without a fingerprint are rejected as
# malformed and fail the scan. A trailing `# comment` is allowed.
#
# Every entry needs a justification. If you add one, say what the fixture is
# and why it has to look like a real credential.

